A cozy evening scene in the style of Vincent van Gogh with swirling brushstrokes and rich, warm colors. A towering stack of weathered technical books and manuals rises organically from a wooden desk, their spines creating a mosaic of deep blues, ochres, and burnt oranges. The books seem to spiral upward like a growing vine, pages gently unfurling at the edges. Through a window behind the desk, the Singapore skyline glimmers with starry night energy, painted with characteristic thick impasto strokes. A warm lamp casts golden, radiating light across the scene, its glow rendered in concentric circles of yellow and amber. The desk surface shows traces of a life of learning—a coffee cup, reading glasses, scattered bookmarks. The entire composition pulses with movement and passionate energy, celebrating the tactile joy of physical books and accumulated wisdom.
